## Environment configuration (tfvars)

### `environments/dev.tfvars`

```hcl
environment            = "dev"
aws_region             = "us-east-1"
db_instance_class      = "db.t3.micro"
db_multi_az            = false
replica_region         = ""            # no CRR in dev
eks_cluster_name       = "dev-cluster"
allow_write            = true

# node group sizing per spec
node_instance_type = "t3.medium"
node_count         = 2
```

### `environments/prod.tfvars`

```hcl
environment            = "prod"
aws_region             = "us-east-1"
replica_region         = "us-west-2"   # enables cross-region replication
db_instance_class      = "db.t3.medium"
db_multi_az            = true
eks_cluster_name       = "prod-cluster"
eks_oidc_provider_arn  = "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:oidc-provider/oidc.eks.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/id/EXAMPLED539D4633E53DE1B71"
allow_write            = true

node_instance_type = "t3.large"
node_count         = 4
```

### Usage — workspaces or tfvars

```bash
# Workspaces: each workspace has independent state → prod changes never touch dev
terraform workspace new dev && terraform workspace select dev
terraform init
terraform plan -var-file=environments/dev.tfvars -out=tfplan
terraform apply tfplan

terraform workspace select prod || terraform workspace new prod
terraform plan -var-file=environments/prod.tfvars -out=tfplan
terraform apply tfplan
```

Alternatively add a small lookup in root `main.tf` so `terraform.workspace` selects the right tfvars automatically via `-var-file`, or use separate state keys per environment.

## Notes on acceptance criteria mapping

| Criterion | Where |
|---|---|
| Bucket versioning + encryption, no public access | `aws_s3_bucket_versioning`, SSE config, public access block |
| RDS deletion protection, backups ≥7d, private | `deletion_protection = true`, retention validation, `publicly_accessible = false`, `prevent_destroy` |
| Secret not in Git | Random-generated master password stored in Secrets Manager (KMS-encrypted); no credentials committed |
| IAM least privilege | Explicit actions only (`s3:GetObject`, etc.), OIDC trust in prod, no wildcard actions |
| Env isolation | Separate workspaces/state + distinct resource naming/prefix per environment |
